{
  "_readme": [
    "Keyword stems per SPOF theme, used by eval/hinge-labels.ts to decide which",
    "of a fixture's expected_spof_themes a produced SPOF landed on.",
    "",
    "GRAMMAR (Q20 — plain substring matching is gone, it fired `rma` inside",
    "'information' and `bot` inside 'both'):",
    "  stem   = whole word, plural tolerated. `bot` hits bot/bots, never both.",
    "  stem*  = prefix at a word start. `verif*` hits verified/verification;",
    "           `position*` hits positioning but NOT pro-position.",
    "  a b    = multi-word, matched across a space or a hyphen, so 'off app' and",
    "           'off-app' are one rule (duplicates are collapsed, not counted twice).",
    "Weight: a stem of 6+ characters counts 2, anything shorter counts 1 — so a",
    "passing `sla` or `bot` cannot outrank a theme the prose actually argues. Stems",
    "that tie are reported as a group; the screen does not pick a winner.",
    "",
    "Stems must stay narrow: a stem that fires on unrelated prose turns every",
    "hinge into the same theme and the drift number goes to zero. If a theme is",
    "added to a golden fixture, add it here or the auto verdict reports 'unmatched'",
    "for that side instead of guessing."
  ],
